WEBVTT

00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:14,860
I'll be meeting with an endocrinologist concerning a spot on my thyroid that was shown to be

00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:21,740
cancerous three years ago and now a new spot has been seen at a PET scan. What are some questions

00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:28,060
or tests that I can ask for with this doctor? I want to avoid the removal of my thyroid.

00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:37,390
Well, I would ask the questions like how big is this spot? Can we keep an eye on it

00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:44,670
and do another test in three months if they're solely going as a PET scan for

00:00:45,390 --> 00:00:50,990
saying that this is another cancerous spot? Are they going to play in doing a biopsy?

00:00:52,110 --> 00:00:57,870
What's the what's the plan of attack with this? Can you see the spot on an ultrasound? Can you see

00:00:57,870 --> 00:01:04,670
the spot on a CT? Can you see the spot on an MRI? How big is this how big is the tuberous area

00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:11,630
that they think is cancer? All those kind of questions. I would also run some tuber marker tests

00:01:11,630 --> 00:01:19,310
to see if there's any other tests that are going to show, give you some objective data on what's

00:01:19,310 --> 00:01:31,150
going on. Again, it's like anything else, you know, ever want to just rely on one test to make

00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:40,270
a life-changing decision.

